<title>SRI LANKA: Walkers up 7.1 pct up on tourism revival.</title>
<headline>Walkers up 7.1 pct up on tourism revival.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Walkers Tours Ltd rose 7.14 percent or 1.50 rupees to 22.50 in early Wednesday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors are buying the share due to the revival in tourism expected this year,&quot; said a local broker. Tourism is seen improving this year due to tight security after several major terrorist attacks in the past two years.</p>
<p>Walkers Tours, a subsidiary of the blue chip John Keells Holdings Ltd, handles the group's inbound tourist traffic.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
